    {
      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": {"en": "Parts of the body"},
      "texto": {
        "en": "In ordinary contexts, when it is clear whose body part you mean, Spanish often uses **el, la, los, las** instead of a possessive: **levanta la mano**, **tengo las piernas cansadas**, **me duele la espalda**. A possessive can be used for emphasis or contrast.\n\n**La mano** is feminine: **la mano derecha**, **las manos frías**.\n\n**Derecho** and **izquierdo** agree with the body part: **el pie derecho**, **la mano derecha**, **el brazo izquierdo**, **la pierna izquierda**.\n\n**El dedo** means a finger or a toe; add **de la mano** or **del pie** to specify: **los dedos de la mano**, **los dedos del pie**."
      }
    },
